  "notes": "The \"Stoner\" sound, and the research's key fact is a workflow one: the flagship beat was written in about fifteen minutes, which keeps layer counts very low. That is what this model encodes. The kick is the sparsest on this bench after Shawty Redd — 1 plus one syncopated 16th, `densityPerBar` [2,4] — fills are sparse (`hihat.fill.prob` 0.35 against the genre's 0.55), there is no pad, and the melody is one bright synth lead with `contour.riff` 0.75 and `phraseBars` weighted 5:1 to two bars. The mid-range is left open for the vocal, so the lead sits at 76–98 and nothing is authored between it and the 808. The mute-and-return transition the research names is `dropOutBeats` at 0.75 over four beats with `switchUpProb` down at 0.05 — the loop itself never changes, only whether it is playing. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium and both interviews cover one record; `session.bpm` and the pitch-count bounds are the inferred parameters. ⚠ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set because the research says the riff's contour supplies all implied harmony and there is no chordal pad. The i–VI family at weight 2 is INFERRED — the research names only the static tonic — and it exists so the generated chord part reaches its distinct-output floor.",
